WEBVTT

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:14.300
Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
aoku nemuru mizu no hoshi ni sotto

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:22.680
Kissing softly the star of water that sleeps in blue,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
kuchizuke shite inochi no hi wo tomosu hito yo

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:31.410
A person who lights the fire of life,

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
toki to iu kin'iro no sazanami wa

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:36.300
The time, the golden ripple,

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
oozora no kuchibiru ni umareta toiki ne

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:45.070
is a sigh from the lips of the sky,

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
kokoro ni uzumoreta

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:49.300
The stars of kindness...

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
yasashisa no hoshitachi ga

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.270
...buried in heart flame up...

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
honoo age yobiau

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:56.440
...and call to each other,

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
namima sasurau nanpasen no you ni

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:03.430
Like wrecked ships wandering on the waves...

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
mou nakanaide ima

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:08.870
Don't cry, any more,

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
anata wo sagashite iru hito ga iru kara

00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:16.240
because now there is a person looking for you,

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
omae ni aitai yo to

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:20.970
Dying to see you...

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.160
The Jupitris continued to make
mysterious moves.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:40.750
Reccoa Londe therefore snuck into
the Jupitris to search into its identity.

00:01:42.900 --> 00:01:46.360
Scirocco saw right through
Reccoa's actions...

00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:49.060
...but for some reason,
allowed her to escape.

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:55.120
Crisis at Side 2

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:17.770
<i>Hurry with the preparations</i>
<i>for the Suit Carrier!</i>

00:02:17.830 --> 00:02:19.270
<i>And lunch, too!</i>

00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:24.870
Captain Bright expresses his regrets for
not being able to take you to Von Braun.

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:27.970
<i>Never mind me.</i>
<i>Right now, all eyes should be on Side 2.</i>

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:30.840
<i>The Titans are trying to crush</i>
<i>a Side 2 colony...</i>

00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:33.610
<i>...and intimidate us A.E.U.G. as a result.</i>

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:37.790
We won't let the Titans have it their way.

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:42.650
We'll keep fighting even while
we're eating.

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:45.950
<i>Looks like I'll be eating in Von Braun.</i>

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:49.090
Here you are. Here's yours.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.150
Here you are.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.330
Here you are, sir.

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.700
Thank you.

00:02:56.770 --> 00:02:58.670
- Katz?
- Hello.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.740
Here you are, Miss Emma.
A pilot's meal for you.

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:05.640
Thank you.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:09.450
It really helps to have someone
take on these jobs, but...!

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.210
And here's your drink.

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:12.850
Thank you.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:15.150
Did you have a chance to say goodbye
to Lieutenant Quattro?

00:03:15.220 --> 00:03:16.160
No.

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:17.620
You're still not too late.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:19.220
Why don't you go to the bridge now?

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:21.060
The lieutenant was saying...

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:25.090
"These days, time spent worrying
is time wasted. Don't waste time."

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.270
But you never know when you'll see
the Lieutenant again.

00:03:28.870 --> 00:03:29.960
That's true.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:33.340
Well, as long as you're aware of it.

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:36.310
Later I'll help you with your
Nemo simulation.

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.640
Thank you very much.

00:03:38.710 --> 00:03:40.680
Later.

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:45.650
<i>He seems grown-up all of a sudden.</i>
<i>What happened?</i>

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:48.250
The Suit Carrier is taking off!

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:50.190
Okay, you're flying on your own.

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:52.020
Take care.

00:03:52.090 --> 00:03:53.620
<i>Please take care of Side 2.</i>

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.190
Rest assured.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:12.750
Shall we follow the Hyaku Shiki on monitor?

00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:14.080
No, that won't be needed!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:15.710
What is it, Samarn?

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:20.050
A laser message from Von Braun City
has been deciphered.

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:21.250
Show me.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.310
Please come to the analysis room.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:24.990
All right.

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:28.190
Torres, catch up on some rest!

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.360
I haven't got anyone to replace you
should you get sick!

00:04:30.430 --> 00:04:31.730
Thank you very much!

00:04:34.600 --> 00:04:36.090
- And?
- Yes.

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.300
The observation unit at
Sweetwater has confirmed that...

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:43.510
...the Alexandria is the battleship
sailing from Side 7 to Side 2.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:45.770
But that's no different than usual.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:48.180
No, but they seem to have
made contact with...

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.220
...a supply vessel
specializing in gases.

00:04:50.450 --> 00:04:51.420
Gases?

00:04:51.950 --> 00:04:53.480
It seems they've obtained G3.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.320
Did you say G3?!

00:04:56.390 --> 00:04:59.380
That's deadlier than cyanide fume!
That's pure poison!

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:02.930
There's a chance they could use it
against the colony.

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:05.500
They're a reincarnation of Zeon!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:06.500
Those damn Titans!

00:05:09.970 --> 00:05:11.910
Don't rush it... Good.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.240
A bit to the right.

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.040
Good morning, Ensign Reccoa.

00:05:18.110 --> 00:05:19.410
Morning!

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:20.240
Hi.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.870
You're up awfully early.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.280
My Rick Dias should be ready
after a simple checkup.

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:26.190
That's great.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:29.750
With this many battles, we may work
ourselves to death just maintaining the suits.

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:33.320
To tell you the truth, Miss Reccoa's
been pressuring me to work on it.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.330
She's just returned from the Jupitris,
but is already working hard...

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.030
...as if she had been on holiday.

00:05:41.370 --> 00:05:42.960
Have you seen Fa?

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.160
Not yet.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.500
I think she was looking after the children.

00:05:46.580 --> 00:05:48.600
That girl! I'll go and bring her here!

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:49.870
It's okay!

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.670
It's <i>not</i> okay!

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:53.210
Isn't it?

00:05:53.280 --> 00:05:55.310
Get ready for some "recreation" again.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.440
Chief Petty Officer Astonaige!

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.620
Ensign Reccoa's asking
if it's operating properly!

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:01.880
It's operating great!!

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:10.530
Four!

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:17.570
There!

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.600
- Let me! Let me!
- No!

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:21.200
- No fair!
- Give it back!

00:06:21.710 --> 00:06:23.230
- It's mine!
- Give it back!

00:06:23.310 --> 00:06:24.280
Shinta!

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:25.350
Qum!

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:26.920
Kamille!

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:28.650
What's going on?

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:30.810
She's not coming.
I'll get you!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.550
Kamille, bring those two here!

00:06:35.360 --> 00:06:37.350
Here I come!

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:38.820
Hey!

00:06:38.890 --> 00:06:40.950
- Stop!
- They're headed your way!

00:06:41.630 --> 00:06:43.560
There's no need for you to come, too!

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:45.220
Oh, well...!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.770
Be quiet!

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:48.770
Shinta! Qum!

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:49.770
No!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.600
I didn't do any...! Ouch.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.900
Hurry and get your clothes on!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:56.340
War could break out anytime, you know!

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.580
- You've got the looks of a pervert.
- N-No way.

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:04.020
I was just wondering
how the children were reacting.

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:07.540
Please tell Ensign Reccoa
that I'll be there shortly.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:10.560
- Hurry and get your clothes on!
- Okay...

00:07:10.630 --> 00:07:12.790
These two are always like this.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:16.030
Want some help the next time?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.120
What's on your mind when you say that?

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.390
Where are you looking?!

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:21.160
- You're asking for it!
- I did nothing!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:21.930
Hey!

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:23.730
Enough is enough!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:24.640
Okay!

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.330
Boy, she's scary.

00:07:29.110 --> 00:07:31.170
You know how to get
to the cafeteria, right?

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.510
When you're done eating, come back here
and keep Haro company!

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.590
What are you looking at?

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.250
You're very forcible, Fa.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:42.420
What do you mean by that?!

00:07:42.490 --> 00:07:44.980
Are you saying I'm not suited to be a pilot?

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.220
With that force,
you'll make a great pilot.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.630
I really think so!

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:51.660
Damn you!

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:54.830
I'm a pilot, too, you know!

00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.750
Side 2 confirmed!

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:12.620
Thanks for coming, all of you!

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:16.050
I've been put in charge
of the mobile suit team...

00:08:16.130 --> 00:08:17.920
...but I've only got one thing to say!

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:21.160
- It's Lieutenant Yazan. Why's he here?
- He said he wouldn't come.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.530
Lieutenant!

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.130
You weren't invited here...

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:26.170
...because you refused
to join this operation!

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:29.640
- We're not here to make fun!
- I know that!

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:33.700
Sorry about that.

00:08:33.780 --> 00:08:34.900
Now...

00:08:34.980 --> 00:08:36.570
...should we face a long war...

00:08:36.650 --> 00:08:38.610
...several hundred colonies
might go down.

00:08:39.320 --> 00:08:43.650
If we can force the A.E.U.G. to surrender
at the cost of only one colony...

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:47.660
...even God would approve this operation.

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:53.820
But the use of gases is prohibited
under the international treaty.

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:56.660
We all want to return home
as soon as we can.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:08:59.830
Now that the Titans control
the Federation Forces...

00:08:59.900 --> 00:09:01.490
...past treaties are as good as void.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.760
You're right!

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:07.140
We want to put a quick end
to this meaningless war!

00:09:07.210 --> 00:09:10.080
And this operation is the fastest
way to achieve that goal.

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:13.280
Should we succeed in this mission...

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.840
...we, the Titans, will have obtained
a basis for taking over Granada.

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:17.750
Exactly.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:20.180
While we're executing this operation...

00:09:20.260 --> 00:09:22.690
...Gryps will be able
to prepare for an attack on Granada.

00:09:23.230 --> 00:09:25.220
We're just a step away!

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:26.760
All units, begin preparations!

00:09:29.370 --> 00:09:31.990
- We're having a squadron meeting!
- Yes, sir!

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.190
- Has your cylinder been checked?!
- Jerid.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.570
This'll be a tough one to swallow
even if you should succeed.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.010
I'm just satisfying the grudges held
by those killed in action.

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.480
All colonies, satisfactory!

00:09:48.550 --> 00:09:51.180
No reports of any intrusion
from the outside!

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:52.920
Not yet?!

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.010
We're connected, Mr. Mayor.

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:58.390
How does the A.E.U.G. expect to protect
all fifty Colonies of Side 2...

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.550
...with just one or two battleships?!

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:03.600
<i>We've also called some reliable</i>
<i>reinforcements! Please rest assured!</i>

00:10:04.270 --> 00:10:07.200
My priority is protecting
the lives of the residents of Side 2!

00:10:07.270 --> 00:10:09.970
I think it best we become allies
with the Titans!

00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.970
<i>There's only one enemy vessel</i>
<i>approaching us! We will protect Side 2!</i>

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.240
But if they use gas on us,
ten to twenty million people could perish!

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.310
Put me in touch with the Titans' ship!

00:10:25.320 --> 00:10:27.520
- Mr. Mayor!
- What is it?

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:29.450
A meteorite!

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.120
Negative! It appears to be a ship!

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.180
It's moving alongside Colony 35!

00:10:51.780 --> 00:10:54.410
- Direct hit on enemy vessel!
- Good!

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:56.920
That would've torn through the armor
of an old model!

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:59.680
- What about enemy mobile suits?!
- Nemos and GMs! Six in all!

00:10:59.820 --> 00:11:00.790
Okay!

00:11:01.020 --> 00:11:04.080
Send out Lieutenant Jerid's gas unit.

00:11:06.630 --> 00:11:08.860
We've lost communication with
the A.E.U.G.'s battleship.

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:12.030
Enemy mobile suits
are heading toward Colony 25!

00:11:13.200 --> 00:11:15.360
Get the Titans online for me!

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:16.430
Mr. Mayor!

00:11:16.510 --> 00:11:17.700
We'll ask for a ceasefire!

00:11:17.770 --> 00:11:20.940
We can't sacrifice the whole colony
just for the principles of one man!

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:24.610
Mr. Mayor! The Titans
have already started attacking us!

00:11:26.120 --> 00:11:27.240
Make him do it!

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:29.970
Wh-What do you think you're doing?!

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:33.390
- Mr. Mayor!
- We're surrendering to the Titans!

00:11:34.120 --> 00:11:36.720
We have a message here
from Colony 1.

00:11:36.790 --> 00:11:38.050
"Request to negotiate".

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:39.790
They can't surrender this way!

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:41.160
This war will never end...

00:11:41.230 --> 00:11:44.170
...unless we show them the consequences
of going against the Titans!

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:46.470
This goes beyond
the fate of one colony!

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.170
But...!

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.300
The Minovsky particles were too dense...

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.310
...not allowing us to receive
incoming communication!

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:54.740
- That's how you'll interpret this!
- Yes, sir!

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:59.180
We're gambling with the sanctity of life
in this battle.

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:15.230
- Has it started?
- Yes, flashes confirmed.

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:16.630
Wireless transmission intercepted!

00:12:16.700 --> 00:12:18.830
The Titans and the colony
are attempting to establish contact!

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.900
Between the colony under attack
and the Titans?

00:12:23.610 --> 00:12:26.630
What'll we do? It looks like we have
a traitor on our hands!

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:28.300
Are our mobile suits within range?!

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:29.370
No, sir.

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:30.910
Not for another five minutes!

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:35.350
Okay, send the Zeta and Methuss out first!
Have the other mobile suits standby!

00:12:37.850 --> 00:12:40.580
Roger! Zeta Gundam, let's do it!

00:12:43.690 --> 00:12:45.220
Methuss, taking off!

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:14.990
There's yet another one!

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:20.150
There's a gas cylinder
attached to the N-pipe of Colony 25!

00:13:20.230 --> 00:13:22.460
I'll inform the people at once!

00:13:23.270 --> 00:13:25.100
Any word from the Titans yet?!

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:27.140
Nothing, sir!

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:30.630
We can aim at it
from either Colony 22 or 26!

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.140
I'll get them to fire at it!

00:13:32.210 --> 00:13:33.040
No!

00:13:33.110 --> 00:13:34.370
You'll also destroy the colony!

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:37.280
But if the gas is released,
all residents will die immediately!

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.440
Are you questioning my orders?!

00:13:39.510 --> 00:13:41.280
Contact the Titans for me!

00:13:41.450 --> 00:13:44.650
If we can negotiate with them,
they'll stop the release of the gas!

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.690
We've detected a different machine!
It's coming from the Moon's direction!

00:13:47.760 --> 00:13:48.720
What?!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:50.550
Two units!

00:13:50.630 --> 00:13:52.320
Commencing anti-air battery!

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.260
I ordered you not to fire!

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:55.390
But...!

00:13:57.770 --> 00:13:59.100
Damn you!

00:13:59.170 --> 00:14:01.230
If they release the gas,
everyone dies!

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:03.870
Battleship also coming from rear!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:05.240
Isn't it an A.E.U.G. ship?

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:06.400
It's the Argama!

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:09.140
- They're asking about the situation.
- Why are they so late?!

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.580
The enemy's already landed
on Colony 25!

00:14:21.790 --> 00:14:23.280
A meteorite?

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.950
No, that's a dummy.
Then it must be the Alexandria!

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.000
If I hit it directly...!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:36.000
Fire at the enemy ship
from this distance?!

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:38.670
I'm going to hit it!

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:49.140
They're here! Progress at battle speed!
Enter anti-air battle!

00:14:55.320 --> 00:14:56.790
We've attracted the enemy!

00:14:57.430 --> 00:14:58.690
To the colony!

00:15:04.200 --> 00:15:06.170
Kamille's headed for Colony 25!

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:07.330
Good.

00:15:07.400 --> 00:15:09.370
We'll line up horizontally
against the enemy!

00:15:09.440 --> 00:15:11.070
Prepare to attack their ship!

00:15:11.140 --> 00:15:12.440
Mobile suit team, taking off!

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.100
Okay! Go!

00:15:18.250 --> 00:15:21.150
Mobile suits, take off!
Catch up with the team from the Argama!

00:15:22.020 --> 00:15:23.850
Gundam Mk. II, taking off!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:26.410
<i>Lieutenant Emma, I want you</i>
<i>to head to Colony 25...</i>

00:15:26.490 --> 00:15:28.480
<i>...to stop them from attaching the G3!</i>

00:15:28.560 --> 00:15:29.390
Roger!

00:15:31.490 --> 00:15:32.690
Katz! Nemo!

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.060
<i>Listen! You're going to cover</i>
<i>the others from the rear!</i>

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:36.290
<i>Don't forget that!</i>

00:15:36.370 --> 00:15:38.030
Roger! Taking off!

00:15:49.180 --> 00:15:50.840
So they <i>do</i> plan to use
the poison gas!

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.350
Zeta Gundam! You're here!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.020
I'll help you!

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:10.190
<i>Mouar! Hurry them up</i>
<i>with the work! We don't have time!</i>

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.360
We've got do something to
stop them!

00:16:28.820 --> 00:16:30.440
Which side will he come out from?

00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.110
This side!

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:35.950
Hate to disappoint you, Kamille!

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:43.690
What an incredible pilot!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:49.630
If it weren't for you...

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:52.200
...we wouldn't have ended up
with this disgraceful operation!

00:16:57.680 --> 00:16:59.650
I can't get any closer to the colony!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.750
This colony's under construction!

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:16.990
Where's Kamille?

00:17:26.270 --> 00:17:27.330
That Gabthley...!

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:28.840
Where will it attack from?

00:17:34.450 --> 00:17:36.080
I figured he might be in here.

00:17:39.020 --> 00:17:40.180
He's here!

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:44.860
I can't pull the trigger!

00:17:55.600 --> 00:17:57.400
A beam saber?!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.210
It's retreating? Why in the world?!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.890
I need to destroy that cylinder!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:17.910
Right there!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:23.730
I did it!

00:18:24.130 --> 00:18:26.290
<i>Katz, go find Kamille!</i>

00:18:26.370 --> 00:18:27.340
Roger!

00:18:40.420 --> 00:18:41.380
Jerid!

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:43.410
Th-These guys!

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:47.120
I won't let Jerid die!

00:18:49.590 --> 00:18:51.960
If you fire from this close,
you'll also get killed!

00:18:52.030 --> 00:18:53.550
<i>You tried to kill Jerid!</i>

00:18:53.630 --> 00:18:55.120
You'll also die!

00:18:59.770 --> 00:19:00.600
Kamille!

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.000
Katz?!

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:04.830
You're not getting away!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:06.970
Stop, Mouar!

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:09.180
Jerid?! But...!

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:12.740
If you want to exploit your luck,
you've got to hold back at times.

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:13.540
Jerid.

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:20.020
You did well to get here in time, Katz!

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:22.820
All I did was abide by
Lieutenant Emma's orders!

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:23.950
<i>Is that right?</i>

00:19:24.030 --> 00:19:27.430
<i>Didn't you feel anything, Katz?</i>
<i>A pressure from something crooked?</i>

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.320
Yes. Very unpleasant.
My stomach is hurting.

00:19:31.430 --> 00:19:32.590
Exactly.

00:19:32.670 --> 00:19:34.640
That's the feeling of a battlefield.

00:19:35.000 --> 00:19:36.490
Remember that and you'll survive.

00:19:43.350 --> 00:19:46.110
What's the matter, Kamille?
Are you all right?

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:48.910
- I almost bought it out there.
- I see.

00:19:48.980 --> 00:19:49.950
Huh?

00:19:54.020 --> 00:19:55.820
Qum! Shinta!

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:56.910
Fa! Right here!

00:19:57.990 --> 00:19:59.720
- There.
- Hey.

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:06.060
Come on, I told you! You mustn't
go into rooms you don't know!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.030
If you don't listen, I'll make you
take twice as many baths!

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:11.140
Got that?!

00:20:11.210 --> 00:20:12.100
Okay!

00:20:13.040 --> 00:20:14.170
Mr. Apolly.

00:20:14.240 --> 00:20:16.110
Have you seen Ensign Reccoa?

00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:17.670
She returned to her room.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:21.910
Not being out there today,
I've got some catching up to do.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:24.110
Keep it up, Fa.

00:20:24.450 --> 00:20:25.420
Yes, sir!

00:20:27.220 --> 00:20:28.880
Fa's so full of spirit.

00:20:28.960 --> 00:20:32.520
Don't you feel a bit better now
that you've seen Fa's smile?

00:20:33.900 --> 00:20:35.160
"Hee hee," he says.

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:36.890
Where are you going?

00:20:36.970 --> 00:20:38.520
I'm going down to Colony 1.

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.030
As Captain Bright's bodyguard.

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:42.540
Mind if I go, too?

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:43.400
Don't see why not.

00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:52.240
I was only worried about the lives
of the citizens.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:55.010
He didn't mean to fire the gun.

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:57.980
The gun was thought to have blanks,
but it was loaded with bullets.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:01.250
It's up to you whether you
believe me, or not.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.150
But if you'll regard this as an accident...

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:07.090
...I'll consider recommending you
for a pay bonus.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.500
- So you want me to keep this to myself.
- I wouldn't say so...!

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:14.070
But you wouldn't want to rattle
the public unnecessarily, would you?

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.060
<i>The captain of the Argama is here.</i>

00:21:18.570 --> 00:21:20.230
Show him in.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.070
Understand?

00:21:30.120 --> 00:21:34.450
I'm here to ask about a transmission
that was sent out from here.

00:21:35.720 --> 00:21:36.820
What is it about?

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:40.060
A transmission was sent out
from this room to the enemy...

00:21:40.130 --> 00:21:42.530
...just after the battle began, am I right?

00:21:43.670 --> 00:21:46.160
Actually, this is somewhat embarrassing...

00:21:46.230 --> 00:21:49.100
...but there was a traitor among our staff.

00:21:49.570 --> 00:21:53.060
In fact, the officer who just left the room
got injured trying to stop him.

00:21:53.640 --> 00:21:54.540
Oh?

00:21:54.610 --> 00:21:57.170
However, I wish you wouldn't be
too harsh on the traitor.

00:21:57.480 --> 00:21:59.500
We're practically confined
inside a cage here.

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:05.180
If a poison gas like G3 were used
against us, we'd have no place to run.

00:22:05.990 --> 00:22:07.580
Very well.

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:11.090
But, mayor, please keep
one thing in mind.

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:15.820
Even if you should attain peace temporarily
by allying with the Titans...

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:18.490
...eventually, you, your citizens,
and all Spacenoids...

00:22:18.570 --> 00:22:21.130
...will end up facing the consequences.

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:27.330
The second homeland of humanity
is a closed world.

00:22:27.540 --> 00:22:32.610
The people of Side 2 know very little
about what happened today.

00:22:47.270 --> 00:22:49.600
Oh, I can't help believing you

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
kanarazu aeru to ano hi kara shinjiteita

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:56.020
I've believed we're sure to meet again ever since that day

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
kitto yobiau kokoro ga areba

00:22:56.070 --> 00:23:01.400
If we have heart, we'll be called together again

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
mugen no Energy yobisamasu

00:23:01.450 --> 00:23:11.790
Awaken the infinite energy

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
aa kizutsukeau mae ni

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:17.420
Before you get hurt

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
dekiru koto sagashite Please

00:23:17.460 --> 00:23:23.510
Find what you can do...Please

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
nagedasanai de kurushii toki koso

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:28.680
Don't throw it away because of this painful age

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
itsuka mita aoi sora wo

00:23:29.390 --> 00:23:32.020
Until the day we gaze up again

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
kitto anata to miageru hi made

00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:39.030
at the blue sky we once saw

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:49.180
Jerid goes into the next battle
prepared to risk his life.

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:54.250
In his background are the strengths
of the people trying to protect him.

00:23:55.630 --> 00:23:59.160
Although Mouar's support provides Jerid
with additional strength...

00:23:59.230 --> 00:24:01.260
...no future seems to be waiting for them.

00:24:01.700 --> 00:24:07.710
Next on Mobile Suit Zeta Gundam,
"Jerid's Desperate Attack".

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Next Episode

00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:12.440
Jerid's Desperate Attack

00:24:07.710 --> 00:24:10.140
You will see the tears of time.
